  "definition_normative_statement": "A Governed Model is a versioned explicit representation of concepts, rules, structures, or behavior with scope, owner, sources, assumptions, validation, lifecycle, and challenge route. It is not automatically an Ontology, runtime, Implementation, truth claim, decision, or admitted authority.",
